course: dictionary
lesson: 313
title: Ancient: very, very old
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Ancient» is an adjective with two meanings. The first is about a time very, very long ago, often thousands of years ago. «The ancient Egyptians built pyramids» tells you about a time far older than your grandparents, or even their grandparents.
explain: The second meaning is playful: «ancient» can mean very old, as when you joke that your brother's phone is ancient. The words around it give the clue. Thousands of years points to the first meaning. A joke about an old thing points to the second.
explain: Look for patterns: «ancient Greece», «ancient ruins», «the ancient world». When ancient comes before a place or a time, it usually means the first meaning. Ask yourself: how long ago did this happen?
fact: «Ancient» means belonging to a time very, very long ago.
fact: «Ancient» can also mean very old, often said as a joke about something old.
fact: Ancient Egypt, Ancient Greece, Ancient Rome and Ancient China are all old civilisations.
fact: «Babylon was one of the largest and most famous cities of the ancient world.»
fact: Scientists call old rocks and fossils ancient to show what the Earth was like in its past.
exercise: «The wise owl idea comes from ancient Greece.» What does ancient mean here? | Very loud | *Very, very long ago | Brand new, made this year | Near the sea
exercise: «When we burn them we release sunlight that ancient plants caught long before the dinosaurs.» Which time does ancient point to? | *A time long before the dinosaurs, very far in the past | Last week | Tomorrow morning | Thousands of years before the dinosaurs
exercise: Mia says her grandad's bike is ancient, though it is only ten years old. What does she mean? | It is a fossil | It is from thousands of years ago | It is a castle | *It is very old, said as a joke
test: «Ancient ruins stood in the desert, covered in sand.» What are ancient ruins? | A new shopping centre | Modern houses still being built | *The remains of buildings from a very long time ago | A type of sandwich
test: Which phrase names a civilisation from long ago? | Last Tuesday | The new shopping centre | Yesterday's football match | *Ancient Egypt
exam: Which sentence uses ancient in its first meaning? | «The ancient bus was shiny and new.» | «My ancient phone takes ages to load.» | *«The ancient Romans built roads that still exist.» | «Ancient cake tasted lovely.»
